r dataset.\n","\n","---\n","\n","###  **What we’ll do next**\n","\n","First, we will explore how **integer embeddings** work.\n","Then, we will learn how deep learning models create their own **neural embeddings** using the `Embedding` layer.\n","\n","This will help you understand the difference between simple word indexing and truly meaningful word representations.\n","\n","---\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Qo32DjNZB58K"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Keras has a convenient library for tokenizing our data and creating integer embeddings.\n","#We will use that.\n","from tensorflow.keras.preprocessing.text import Tokenizer\n","\n","tokenizer = #initliaze the Tokenizer object"],"metadata":{"id":"QoshbgTIptHe"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","\n","\n","###  **What is the `oov_token` parameter inside the `Tokenizer` object?**\n","\n","\n","Answer :\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ErGYara1DrWK"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#fit the tokenizer on our word corpus which we got from applying text_transform method\n"],"metadata":{"id":"4foSPaV6q_Q_"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# convert the text to sequences"],"metadata":{"id":"cVz-VzBTEpEs"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#if all goes well this is what it should look like\n","sequences[:10]"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"Vil7ZAG6rbJQ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1763414335033,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":436,"user":{"displayName":"Pratham Kitawat","userId":"02535698713194553946"}},"outputId":"04dbbf10-111f-4e4f-cd5f-189c31d9b0c0"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["[[7,\n","  982,\n","  366,\n","  18,\n","  2005,\n","  228,\n","  1357,\n","  133,\n","  124,\n","  534,\n","  143,\n","  2,\n","  2,\n","  6,\n","  36,\n","  44,\n","  1172,\n","  2005,\n","  6510,\n","  14099,\n","  27,\n","  483,\n","  104,\n"